    "recommendations": "• Install a reflective address marker at the driveway entrance so responders can confirm the correct property from the road.\n• Mark the driveway entrance with reflective posts on both sides to make the single access point visible at night or in reduced visibility conditions.\n• Clear a turnaround area near the main residence large enough for emergency vehicles to reverse direction without backing the full length of the driveway.\n• Keep the access drive free of parked vehicles so emergency vehicles can reach the residence without obstruction.\n• Trim vegetation along both sides of the access drive to maintain clearance for wide emergency vehicles.\n• Cut back dense vegetation near the detached structure so responders can reach and move around it without obstruction.\n• Mark or identify the pool area with a visible indicator at the perimeter fence so responders are aware of its location during nighttime or low-visibility operations.\n• Keep perimeter fence gates unlocked or secured with a single padlock to allow responders to move between areas without delay.\n• Thin scattered vegetation in open terrain areas that could slow or block responder movement between the residence and detached structure.\n• Post a simple site map at the driveway entrance showing the locations of the main residence, detached structure, pool area, and any locked gates to help responders orient quickly on arrival."
  },
