    "recommendations": "• Trim tree branches that hang close to or over the house and any outbuildings.\n• Thin shrubs scattered near the house to create open gaps between individual plants.\n• Remove shrubs growing directly against the base of the structure.\n• Thin trees within the cluster nearest to the house to reduce the amount of vegetation in that area.\n• Clear dead or dry material from within shrub groupings near the house.\n• Keep low branches on trees near the house trimmed up from the ground.\n• Maintain open spacing between the irrigated landscape plantings and the exterior walls of the house.\n• Trim overhanging branches along the full length of the driveway so vehicles can pass without obstruction.\n• Keep the driveway surface clear of fallen branches, leaf litter, and debris that could block access.\n• Mark the driveway entrance clearly so it is easy to locate from the road, supporting quick access by emergency vehicles.\n• Keep shrubs along the driveway trimmed back so they do not narrow the travel lane or reduce visibility.\n• Keep the area around any outbuildings or secondary structures clear of shrub growth on all sides."
